    "High, low and urgent low glucose alerts are issued by %1$@ according to its own alert settings. Review them so they match what you had in the Dexcom app." : {
      "comment" : "Glucose alerts paragraph of the alerts hand-off page (1: appName)"
    },
    "Hold the applicator by its narrow end and unscrew the wide cap." : {
      "comment" : "Apply step 3: unscrew the cap"
    },
    "Hold the sensor down for 10 seconds, then rub firmly around the patch three times." : {
      "comment" : "Apply step 6: secure the patch"
    },
    "Holding the colored tab, center the overpatch over the sensor and press it on." : {
      "comment" : "Overpatch step B"
    },
    "hour" : {
      "comment" : "Unit after a remaining-time number, singular"
    },
    "hours" : {
      "comment" : "Unit after a remaining-time number, plural"
    },
    "How to Apply a Sensor" : {
      "comment" : "Button title opening the step-by-step application guide\nNavigation title of the step-by-step application guide"
    },
    "hr" : {
      "comment" : "Abbreviated hours unit after a remaining-time number\nUnit after the hours-since-last-reading number"
    },
    "I've Removed It" : {
      "comment" : "Button title to confirm the Dexcom app was deleted or offloaded"
    },
    "If iOS asks to pair with the sensor, tap Pair." : {
      "comment" : "Hint about the system Bluetooth pairing prompt during G7 pairing"
    },
    "If the Dexcom app has used the sensor you are pairing, wait about 15 minutes after it last connected. A sensor it has never used can be paired right away." : {
      "comment" : "Dexcom app warning: the lease wait applies only if the Dexcom app has used this sensor"
    },
    "In Settings › Focus, open each Focus you use and add %1$@ to its allowed apps." : {
      "comment" : "Advice bullet: focus allowed apps (1: appName)"
    },
    "In Settings › General › iPhone Storage. Removes the app but keeps its data, so reinstalling restores it." : {
      "comment" : "Detail of the option to offload the Dexcom app"
    },
    "In Settings › Notifications › %1$@, turn on Time Sensitive Notifications." : {
      "comment" : "Advice bullet: time sensitive setting (1: appName)"
    },
    "In this mode %1$@ can only read glucose while the Dexcom G7 app is installed and running a session. Pair the sensor directly instead, or reinstall the Dexcom app." : {
      "comment" : "Body of the settings warning when the Dexcom app is missing in eavesdropping mode (1: appName)"
    },
    "INSERT SENSOR" : {
      "comment" : "Section label above the insert-sensor steps"
    },
    "Keep the applicator until you have paired: the 4-digit pairing code is printed on it. Dispose of it as sharps afterwards." : {
      "comment" : "Apply step 5 note: keep the applicator for its code"
    },
    "Keep your phone near the sensor. A sensor that was recently used by the Dexcom app or another phone can take up to 15 minutes to become available; this screen will keep looking." : {
      "comment" : "Pairing guidance while scanning"
    },
    "Keep your ringer on. Silent mode mutes every sound that is not a Critical Alert." : {
